<article class="env-lemma" id="0BXH">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BXH">Lemma <span data-tag="0BXH">31.16.9</span>.</a> Let $Z \subset X$ be a closed subscheme of a Noetherian scheme. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$Z$ has no embedded points, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
every irreducible component of $Z$ has codimension $1$ in $X$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
every local ring $\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$, $x \in Z$ is a UFD or $X$ is regular. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then $Z$ is an effective Cartier divisor. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $D = \sum a_ i D_ i$ be as in Lemma <a href="/tag/0AGB" data-tag="0AGB">31.16.8</a> where $D_ i \subset Z$ are the irreducible components of $Z$. If $D \to Z$ is not an isomorphism, then $\mathcal{O}_ Z \to \mathcal{O}_ D$ has a nonzero kernel sitting in codimension $\geq 2$. This would mean that $Z$ has embedded points, which is forbidden by assumption (1). Hence $D \cong Z$ as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>